course: dictionary
lesson: 9366
title: Sponsorship
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Sponsorship is a noun, and it is uncountable, so you say some sponsorship, not a sponsorship. Look at the words around it to find its meaning. «Sponsorship means people promise to give money to a charity if someone completes a challenge.» The words money, promise and charity are your clues.
explain: Sponsorship can also mean a company paying for an event, a team or an activity, often so that its name is seen. A company logo on a football shirt is one example. Phrases like sponsorship deal and under the sponsorship of show you how the word is used.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. Does «people promise to give money to a charity if someone completes a challenge» still make sense with sponsorship's meaning in place? If it does, you have understood the word.
fact: Sponsorship is money or support given to pay for something, often in return for advertising.
fact: In a sponsored run, friends promise to pay money to a charity for each lap or mile someone completes.
fact: A sponsorship deal is an agreement: the sponsor pays, and in return gets its name advertised.
fact: Sponsorship can also mean officially supporting someone, such as a club member or a person moving to a new country.
exercise: «Sponsorship means people promise to give money to a charity if someone completes a challenge.» What does sponsorship mean in this sentence? | A kind of holiday for families | *Money promised to a charity when someone completes a challenge | A type of sport played on ice | A sign on a shop window
exercise: Maya's friend says, «We got sponsorship from the local bakery.» What does this mean? | The bakery was closed all day | *The bakery gave money or support to the event, often to advertise its name | The bakery moved to a new town | The children baked a cake for the teacher
exercise: Why might a company's logo be on a football shirt? | The team is playing a match at the company's office | The shirt is very old | The company made the shirt by hand | *The company is sponsoring the team, paying for it and advertising its name
test: In «Ella got sponsorship from her club to train abroad», what does sponsorship mean? | *Official support from her club | A type of food | A promise to walk ten miles | A fine for bad behaviour
test: Which sentence uses sponsorship correctly? | *We raised some sponsorship for the read-a-thon. | The sponsorship is a very tall boy. | We sponsorship the read-a-thon with three friends. | The sponsorship walked very quickly to the field.
exam: Mia says sponsorship is just a fancy word for a gift. Which answer is best? | Sponsorship means a birthday present from a friend | Sponsorship means a prize for winning a race | *Sponsorship means money or support given for an event or charity, often in return for advertising or promised when a challenge is completed | Sponsorship means a rule in a game
